      "title": "Gutenberg Health Study (GHS)",
      "url_or_doi": "https://www.unimedizin-mainz.de/GHS/uebersicht/overview.html",
      "justification": "The Gutenberg Health Study is a prospective population-based cohort study initiated in 2007 by the University Medical Center Mainz in Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany. Examining over 15,000 adults aged 35–74 during the 2000s and 2010s, it collects detailed health data on medical conditions (cardiovascular, cancer, eye diseases, metabolic, mental health), medication and treatments, adult vaccination coverage, preventive checkups, screening participation, smoking, alcohol, diet, physical activity, blood pressure metrics, and demographic characteristics."
    },
    {
      "title": "German Health Update (GEDA 2019/2020-EHIS) - Robert Koch Institute",
      "url_or_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7214473",
      "justification": "GEDA is a repeated population-based health survey conducted by the Robert Koch Institute (RKI) covering all German federal states, including Rhineland-Palatinate. It collects standardized data on adult health outcomes, disease prevalence, medication usage, adult vaccination coverage, preventive checkups and cancer screenings, lifestyle risk factors (smoking, alcohol, diet, physical activity), blood pressure awareness, health risk perceptions, and detailed sociodemographic characteristics."
    }
  ]
